;; M4S named fallback (docs/m4s-contract.md): a negation edge INSIDE the
;; struct cone.  `in` feeds the struct constructor positively and the
;; complement rule negatively, so every edit's cone crosses ~; negation
;; stays refused by name under M4S (M4N owns anti-deltas), and the struct
;; relation keeps the cone outside every counted route -- both signs must
;; settle through clear-and-rerun.
;;
;; With in = {(1,1), (2,5)}:
;;   out     = { (pair 1 1) (pair 2 5) }
;;   blocked = keys K in {1,2,3} with NO in(K,K) = { 2, 3 }
;; Deleting in(1,1): out = { (pair 2 5) } (1 live id + 1 tombstone) and
;; blocked GROWS to { 1, 2, 3 } -- the complement recomputes exactly.

struct (pair int int)
table (in int int)
table (key int)
table (out pair)
table (blocked int)

rule (key 1) (key 2) (key 3)

rule
(in X Y)
-->
(out (pair X Y))

rule
(key K)
~(in K K)
-->
(blocked K)
